1. Title

Minimum Cost Hospital Fiber Optic Network Using Prim's Algorithm

2. Introduction

A hospital has different departments such as Emergency, ICU, Laboratory, Pharmacy and Administration. These departments need a fast communication network. Fiber optic cables are used to connect these departments. Prim's Algorithm helps to connect all departments with minimum installation cost.

3. Problem Statement

To represent hospital blocks and possible fiber optic connections with installation costs, and apply Prim's Algorithm to determine the minimum-cost communication network.

4. Objectives

To understand the concept of Minimum Spanning Tree.
To connect all hospital departments.
To minimize fiber optic cable installation costs.
To implement Prim's Algorithm using C++.
To design an efficient communication network.

5. Algorithm

1.Start the program.
2.Create a weighted graph of hospital departments.
3.Select the starting vertex.
4.Find the minimum-cost edge.
5.Add the selected edge to the MST.
6.Repeat until all vertices are connected.
7.Calculate the total minimum cost.
8.Display the result.
9.Stop the program.


6. Advantages

Reduces installation costs.
Provides fast communication.
Avoids unnecessary cable connections.
Connects all hospital departments.
Saves time and resources.

7. Applications

Hospital communication systems.
ICU monitoring systems.
Laboratory data transfer.
Digital medical records.
Emergency communication.

8. Future Scope

Smart hospital networks.
IoT-based healthcare systems.
Improved data security.
Connecting new hospital buildings.
High-speed medical data transfer.


9. Conclusion

Prim's Algorithm helps to design a minimum-cost fiber optic network for hospitals. It connects all departments without unnecessary connections and reduces installation costs. It provides an efficient and reliable communication network.


